From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 14:07:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 200/225] arm64: dts: ums512: raise idle injection cap to 80%

50% left the governor short of authority: the die was already sitting near
100C, only 10C under the critical trip, when injection was running deeper
than that. The cap is a bound rather than a target - step_wise ramps one
state per 100ms polling interval and settles at the lowest state that holds
temperature - so a higher ceiling costs nothing until it is actually needed.

Only state 100 is unusable, where run time is exactly zero; 80 still gives
2.5ms of execution per 12.5ms period, which keeps scheduling, ssh and input
alive. Heavy titles now throttle rather than hitting the critical trip.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
